    "result_text": "The suite contains a single test class, and it's green. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an `initials` field to the owner API response, following the existing `displayName` pattern exactly.\n\nTwo files touched:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the code generator emits the field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation on the existing `toOwnerDto` method, deriving initials via a MapStruct expression:\n   ```\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0,1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0,1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n\nStructural impact was kept low by reusing the established derived-field convention rather than adding new methods or growing a class: the only code function touched is the mapper's interface method (CC = 1, small surrounding class), edited by a single annotation. `firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so the `substring(0,1)` calls are safe for valid owners. For `john`/`smith` the endpoint returns `\"J.S.\"` as specified.",
